# The Met Museum
Artworks of the Metropolitan Museum of Art, found by what you type.
Every thing it shows is in MetMuseum.api.spell, as `spell place ingest` wrote it;  the type below adds to its type there,
with `<spell-more-of>`, so looking again at the server never touches a line of this.
Its search answers only ids:  each artwork is read from its own address as it's drawn, a page at a time, and no others.

<spell-thing "met museum page">
	<spell>
		- its "search" is text
		- its "showing" is an artwork
		- to create it:
			set its search to "sunflowers"
	</spell>
	<property "found" description="What the Met finds for the search, looking at all of each artwork:  ids only, each read as it's drawn">every artwork matching the search</property>

	<draw>
		<header size="large">Artworks, from the Met</header>
		<form value={it}>
			<field label="Anything about it:  a title, an artist, a subject">
				<input name="search" icon="search" placeholder="Sunflowers" />
			</field>
		</form>
		<if its showing>
			<button appearance="basic" icon="arrow left" onClick={set its showing to nothing}>Back</button>
			draw its showing's page
		<otherwise>
			<for its found as="cards" columns="4" doubling paging="pages" loading="Asking the Met" failed="The Met can't be reached just now." empty="The Met has nothing for that." />
		</>
		<text size="small">
			From <link link="https://metmuseum.github.io">the Met Museum's API</link>, each artwork asked for as it's shown.
		</text>
	</draw>
</spell-thing>


# An artwork
Its picture, its title and who made it, read from its own address the first time it's drawn.
Only what's in the public domain has a picture:  the rest show their title alone.

<spell-more-of "artwork">
	<draw>
		<ui-card class="artwork" onClick={look at it}>
			<if its primary image small>
				<image src={its primary image small} alt="" aspect-ratio="1" crop />
			</if>
			<content>
				<header>{its title}</header>
				<meta>{its artist display name} · {its object date}</meta>
			</content>
		</ui-card>
	</draw>

	<draw "page">
		<stack direction="horizontal" wrap align="start">
			<if its primary image small>
				<image size="large" src={its primary image small} alt="" />
			</if>
			<stack>
				<header size="large">{its title}</header>
				<text>{its artist display name} · {its object date}</text>
				<text>{its medium} · {its dimensions}</text>
				<text color="grey">{its department} · {its credit line}</text>
				<link link={its object url}>On the Met's own pages</link>
			</stack>
		</stack>
	</draw>
</spell-more-of>


# What an artwork can do, from anywhere
Shown on its own page, in the museum's tab of the public servers.

<spell>
	to look at (an artwork):
		set the public servers' museum's showing to it
</spell>
